{"type":"assistant","uuid":"ef890648-4e81-4f88-ad14-6b950ab227bb","session_id":"572d68c5-ec5a-4a5a-b3b8-523e2c78c78e","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"ef890648-4e81-4f88-ad14-6b950ab227bb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is complete. Here's a summary of what was wrong and what I changed:\n\n**Bugs found in `ExerciseDialog.java`:**\n\n1. **Primary crash bug (all checkboxes):** Every checkbox handler called `Integer.valueOf(...)` or `Double.valueOf(...)` directly on the EditText text without checking if it was empty. When a checkbox was checked but the corresponding field was empty, `Integer.valueOf(\"\")` threw a `NumberFormatException`, crashing the app.\n\n2. **Secondary bug (line 70):** The Back section had a copy-paste bug — `if(isAngnleActivated)` instead of `if(isBackActivated)`, meaning the Back position was only parsed when the Angle checkbox was checked.\n\n3. **Typo (line 56):** Variable named `isAngnleActivated` instead of `isAngleActivated`.\n\n**Fix applied:**\n- Added `parseIntOrZero()` and `parseDoubleOrZero()` helper methods that safely handle empty strings and invalid input by returning a default value of `0` instead of throwing exceptions.\n- Replaced all direct `Integer.valueOf()` / `Double.valueOf()` calls with these safe helpers.\n- Fixed the typo `isAngnleActivated` → `isAngleActivated`.\n- Fixed the Back section condition from `isAngnleActivated` → `isBackActivated`.\n\nThe project compiles successfully with `./gradlew clean assembleDebug`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31419,"output_tokens":601,"cache_read_input_tokens":29344,"total_tokens":32020}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"0103fcb9-a110-4a23-80b3-9737d33781aa","session_id":"572d68c5-ec5a-4a5a-b3b8-523e2c78c78e","is_error":false,"duration_ms":44886,"duration_api_ms":29141,"num_turns":7,"result":"\n\nThe fix is complete. Here's a summary of what was wrong and what I changed:\n\n**Bugs found in `ExerciseDialog.java`:**\n\n1. **Primary crash bug (all checkboxes):** Every checkbox handler called `Integer.valueOf(...)` or `Double.valueOf(...)` directly on the EditText text without checking if it was empty. When a checkbox was checked but the corresponding field was empty, `Integer.valueOf(\"\")` threw a `NumberFormatException`, crashing the app.\n\n2. **Secondary bug (line 70):** The Back section had a copy-paste bug — `if(isAngnleActivated)` instead of `if(isBackActivated)`, meaning the Back position was only parsed when the Angle checkbox was checked.\n\n3. **Typo (line 56):** Variable named `isAngnleActivated` instead of `isAngleActivated`.\n\n**Fix applied:**\n- Added `parseIntOrZero()` and `parseDoubleOrZero()` helper methods that safely handle empty strings and invalid input by returning a default value of `0` instead of throwing exceptions.\n- Replaced all direct `Integer.valueOf()` / `Double.valueOf()` calls with these safe helpers.\n- Fixed the typo `isAngnleActivated` → `isAngleActivated`.\n- Fixed the Back section condition from `isAngnleActivated` → `isBackActivated`.\n\nThe project compiles successfully with `./gradlew clean assembleDebug`.","usage":{"input_tokens":176883,"output_tokens":3876,"cache_read_input_tokens":144624,"total_tokens":180759},"permission_denials":[]}
